  "summary_en": "US TSA regulation (49 CFR Part 1552) establishing the Flight Training Security Program: security threat assessments for alien flight candidates, provider registration, Security Coordinators, security awareness training, recordkeeping and event notification. It expressly excludes unmanned aircraft training. It has no AI or robotics content.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Providers may train only US citizens/nationals, DoD endorsees, or candidates with a TSA Determination of Eligibility",
   "Candidates submit biometric data and fees for a TSA security threat assessment including an FBI criminal history check",
   "Providers must designate a Security Coordinator and give employees security awareness training",
   "Providers must notify TSA of flight training events via the FTSP Portal",
   "Flight training excludes unmanned aircraft instruction"
  ],
